Requirements: 25   with obligations: 24   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] The completion verdict accounts for how much of the mandate the review
    actually covered, so a review that spoke to only part of the mandate cannot report
    that it found no material gaps.
    -> completion-verdict-reflects-coverage  [functional/explicit]
       The completion verdict accounts for how much of the mandate the review actually
       covered, so partial coverage cannot be reported as having no material gaps.

[constraint-01] The share of the mandate's requirements that produced at least one
    obligation is recorded on the completion result.
    -> record-share-on-completion-result  [functional/explicit]
       The share of the mandate's requirements that produced at least one obligation is
       recorded on the completion result.

[constraint-02] A requirement that produced no obligation lowers the recorded share.
    -> lower-recorded-share-for-no-obligation  [functional/explicit]
       A requirement that produced no obligation lowers the recorded share.

[constraint-03] A review whose recorded share is short of the whole mandate is never
    reported as free of material gaps.
    -> short-share-never-free-of-gaps  [functional/explicit]
       A review whose recorded share is short of the whole mandate is never reported as
       free of material gaps.

[constraint-04] A share short of the whole mandate only ever bounds the verdict and
    never raises it, so a review that covers less of the mandate never reports a better
    result than the same review covering more of it.
    -> short-share-only-bounds-verdict  [functional/explicit]
       A share short of the whole mandate only ever bounds the verdict and never raises
       it, so a review that covers less of the mandate never reports a better result
       than the same review covering more of it.

[constraint-05] A requirement that states no checkable expectation does not lower the
    recorded share.
    -> no-checkable-expectation-does-not-lower-share  [functional/explicit]
       A requirement that states no checkable expectation does not lower the recorded
       share.

[constraint-06] Task-file text that produced no requirement at all bounds the verdict in
    the same way as a requirement that produced no obligation.
    -> no-requirement-text-bounds-verdict-like-no-obligation  [functional/explicit]
       Task-file text that produced no requirement at all bounds the verdict in the same
       way as a requirement that produced no obligation.

[constraint-07] The completion verdict states the share it was derived under and names
    the requirements that produced nothing.
    -> verdict-states-share-and-empty-requirements  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       The completion verdict states the share it was derived under and names the
       requirements that produced nothing.

[constraint-08] The completion verdict is derived from the review's own recorded state
    without consulting a model.
    -> verdict-derived-from-recorded-state-without-model  [functional/explicit]
       The completion verdict is derived from the review's own recorded state without
       consulting a model.

[constraint-09] Two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical review
    state.
    -> byte-identical-task-text-yields-byte-identical-review-state  [regression/explicit]
       Two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical review state.

[constraint-10] Tests issue no live model calls.
    -> no-live-model-calls-in-tests  [functional/explicit]
       Tests issue no live model calls.

[exclusion-01] Whether a requirement that produced no obligation was correctly declined;
    the stated reason is taken at face value and not re-judged.
    -> no-rejudging-declined-no-obligation-requirements  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not re-judge whether a requirement that produced no obligation
       was correctly declined; the stated reason is taken at face value.

[exclusion-02] How stable decomposition is from one run to the next, which is #193.
    -> no-change-to-decomposition-stability-from-run-to-run  [regression/explicit]
       The change does not alter how stable decomposition is from one run to the next.

[exclusion-03] Measuring how accurate decomposition is, which is #211.
    -> no-change-to-decomposition-accuracy-measurement  [regression/explicit]
       The change does not alter how decomposition accuracy is measured.

[exclusion-04] How finely a single requirement is split into obligations, which is #117.
    -> no-change-to-requirement-splitting-granularity  [regression/explicit]
       The change does not alter how finely a single requirement is split into
       obligations.

[exclusion-05] Whether obligation identifiers are stable across task-file edits, which
    is #231.
    -> no-change-to-obligation-identifier-stability-across-edits  [compatibility/explicit]
       The change does not alter whether obligation identifiers are stable across task-
       file edits.

[exclusion-06] How an obligation's evidence is rated, which is #180.
    -> no-change-to-obligation-evidence-rating  [regression/explicit]
       The change does not alter how an obligation's evidence is rated.

[exclusion-07] Which tests are discovered, and which obligations they are mapped to.
    -> no-change-to-test-discovery-and-obligation-mapping  [compatibility/explicit]
       The change does not alter which tests are discovered or which obligations they
       are mapped to.

[completion-01] Implementation
    -- no obligation, deliberately
       A standalone section marker with no requirement under it.

